    <string name="compartment_about_tor">About Tor</string>
    <string name="compartment_tor_desc">Tor sends your traffic through three volunteer relays, so sites see a Tor exit node instead of your real address. It is slower than a direct connection, and some sites block Tor exit nodes.</string>
    <string name="compartment_verification">Verification</string>
    <string name="compartment_tor_check">Check this browser uses Tor</string>
    <string name="compartment_tor_check_sub">Opens check.torproject.org</string>
    <string name="compartment_i2p_keep_title">Keep I2P running in the background</string>
    <string name="compartment_i2p_keep_sub">Stay connected to the I2P network even after leaving the I2P compartment, so it reconnects instantly.</string>
    <string name="compartment_i2p_addressbook">Addressbook subscriptions</string>
    <string name="compartment_i2p_addressbook_sub">Fetch hosts.txt lists from inside I2P so .i2p sites (reg.i2p, stats.i2p…) resolve automatically instead of needing a jump service. Applies next time I2P starts.</string>
    <string name="compartment_about_i2p">About I2P</string>
    <string name="compartment_i2p_desc">I2P is a peer-to-peer anonymous network. .i2p eepsites load directly inside I2P; ordinary websites are routed through a public I2P outproxy. Building tunnels can take a minute on first use.</string>
    <string name="compartment_normal_desc">A direct connection with no anonymity layer — the fastest option, but websites see your real IP address. Switch to Tor or I2P from the network button when you want to browse privately.</string>

